    "page": "https://opengameart.org/content/textured-cute-monster-pack",
    "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
    "note": "Wave-1 row 103 named the Ghost from Quaternius's poly.pizza \"Cute Monsters\" set (8 clips incl. Flying_Idle, Fast_Flying, Punch); poly.pizza is behind a Cloudflare challenge and Quaternius's Google Drive is quota-blocked, so that flying version is unreachable. This is the Ghost from the same author's Textured Cute Monster Pack (Aug 2020) on OpenGameArt: same character family, ten ground clips, no flying clips. Its .blend expects Ghost_Texture.png beside itself; the pipeline relinks it from the zip's Textures folder. The painted grey texture is flattened to 16 clusters: body greys -> body, the near-black eye, brow and mouth clusters -> dark, the eye catchlight -> glint, the purple tongue -> tongue, the cream teeth -> teeth. The #666666 cluster is shared by the lower rim of each eye and a patch low on the body's side, so it goes to body (a pale lower lid) rather than leave a dark stain on the side. Ground: this ghost has no tail; its flat, open base rests on the ground and every clip hops, rocks or tips on it, so it touches rather than hovers; Walk, Jump, Death, HitRecieve, Dance and Yes clamp to the ground (the tumble in Death would otherwise sink 16 cm). For a floating ghost, lift the root in the film. Height 0.8 m is a chibi choice: a ghost has no real size, and 0.8 m puts the big-eyed blob at a child's height, about the waist of a 1.7 m adult, matching the pack's cute scale."
  },
